license: Apache-2.0

abstract: >
  Lean 4 formalization of fragment-relative common ground in Structural
  Explainability. Given a bounded referential fragment, the theory classifies
  frameworks by the valuations they permit on the fragment's vocabulary. A
  framework is neutral on a vocabulary exactly when it is jointly satisfiable
  with every satisfiable theory over that vocabulary, and every framework either
  is neutral or conflicts with some such theory. When admissibility is the only
  condition on frameworks, only valid commitment sets are framework-compatible,
  so common ground for a nontrivial fragment requires an explicit condition on
  frameworks. The theory instantiates the Neutral Substrate consequence system
  with classical propositional logic. Results are relative to a stated fragment
  and framework class and make no claim about the full class of admissible
  frameworks.

keywords:
